{"total_count": 1, "workflow_runs": [{"actor": {"avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}", "gravatar_id": "", "html_url": "https://github.com/nickderobertis", "id": 19440155, "login": "nickderobertis", "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos", "site_admin": false, "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions", "type": "User", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis", "user_view_type": "public"}, "artifacts_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/actions/runs/38829119610/artifacts", "cancel_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/actions/runs/38829119610/cancel", "check_suite_id": 105229293155, "check_suite_node_id": "CS_kwDOTx8aUc8AAAAYgCeWYw", "check_suite_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/check-suites/105229293155", "conclusion": "success", "created_at": "2026-10-16T00:22:30Z", "display_title": "Published smoke", "event": "workflow_run", "head_branch": "main", "head_commit": {"author": {"email": "whoopnip@gmail.com", "name": "Nick DeRobertis"}, "committer": {"email": "noreply@github.com", "name": "GitHub"}, "id": "e6d813cd7b267c09c4e8ba83f74a2ffc52691ee0", "message": "fix(test): end every process a test spawns before the test returns (#922)\n\n## What\n\nMake shared test-fixture teardown terminate and wait for harness doubles\nand their descendants, with PID-based regression coverage. CI now fails\nand reruns tests that leak output handles; the leak-detection regression\nalso waits for its own deliberately leaked processes to exit.\n\nRaise the cross-platform gate\u2019s timeout to 180 minutes and its job\u2019s to\n220 minutes. Give the readjust store journey 600 seconds and other\nWindows tests 540 seconds to accommodate the slower runner image; other\nplatforms retain their existing limits. Prevent the maintenance failure\nfixture from repeating its command during the same phase on slow hosts.\n\n## Why\n\nLeftover processes keep the required Windows check\u2019s output open after\ntests pass, forcing two-hour reruns and blocking correct changes. This\nrepeatedly blocked #904\u2019s fix for 30\u201350 GB of daily Codex plugin catalog\ndownloads. Cleanup lets the check finish when its work ends; the\nincreased limits give the existing test tiers time to complete.\n\n## Additional info\n\nWindows containment includes orphaned descendants. Unix cleanup covers\nprocesses still descended from the test at teardown and continues\nwaiting for those it finds even if their parents exit; processes\norphaned to init before teardown remain outside that guarantee.\n\nThe macOS regression assertion failed because a Linux-only `/proc` probe\ntreated exited zombies as running. The probe now uses `ps`, and teardown\naccepts macOS\u2019s unclassified `?` process states.\n\nThe leak-detection regression previously passed on Linux but was itself\nmarked `LEAK-FAIL` on Windows because its inner runs\u2019 sleepers inherited\nthe outer test\u2019s output handles. It now waits for their recorded PIDs to\nexit and asserts that none remain on every supported platform.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nick <nick@U-17UN402ICR95C.workspaces.hellopatient.internal>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>", "timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:18:40Z", "tree_id": "0b926f2deb13bd60c49352f5e71817d27f950fd3"}, "head_repository": {"archive_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/{archive_format}{/ref}", "assignees_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/assignees{/user}", "blobs_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/git/blobs{/sha}", "branches_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/branches{/branch}", "collaborators_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/collaborators{/collaborator}", "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/comments{/number}", "commits_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/commits{/sha}", "compare_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/compare/{base}...{head}", "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/contents/{+path}", "contributors_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/contributors", "deployments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/deployments", "description": "Compose a task DAG over oneagentgraph and onevcs: one merged event stream, a pluggable executor seam.", "downloads_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/downloads", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/events", "fork": false, "forks_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/forks", "full_name": "nickderobertis/onepipeline", "git_commits_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/git/commits{/sha}", "git_refs_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/git/refs{/sha}", "git_tags_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/git/tags{/sha}", "hooks_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/hooks", "html_url": "https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline", "id": 1327438417, "issue_comment_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/